[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=Planar URP65 / URP65-T RS-232 control.\\Protocol: Planar UltraRes||1
  Cmn2=P Series RS232 User Manual 020-1408-02B.\\That manual covers URP65||1
  Cmn3=and URP65-T. This module has not been tried on a live display.\\
  Cmn4=\\19200 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, no flow control.
  Cmn5=\\Use a straight-through cable to a Crestron COM port.\\Display||1
  Cmn6=pin 2 is Tx, pin 3 is Rx, pin 5 is ground.\\RS-232 works in standby||1
  Cmn7=only when Power Down Mode is Networked Standby or Fast Startup.\\
  Cmn8=\\Commands end with a carriage return. The display answers with||1
  Cmn9=a colon:\\DISPLAY.POWER=ON\\DISPLAY.POWER:ON\\\\Sources are HDMI.
  Cmn10=1, HDMI.2, HDMI.3, HDMI.4, DP, DP.2, and VGA.\\There is no USB-C||1
  Cmn11=input and no OPS input on this model.\\\\Reset_User_Settings sends||1
  Cmn12=RESET(USER). That clears user settings.
[END]
